EF AI Workspace (#189): sidebar v2, owner-approved 2026-10-24 («اعتمد ونفذه بدقة») after comparing ChatGPT, Claude,
Gemini and DeepSeek.

- Column (UnifiedSidebar/EfSidebarColumn.tsx): «New chat», then Projects, Skills and Documents (the files panel) with
  their tints; «More» with memory, bookmarks, ready commands (prompts) and any other panel the deployment enables; under
  a line, the chat search and the active panel (the history, Pinned first). Admins also find the assistants marketplace,
  the agent builder and the parameters in «More», marked «للمسؤول».
- Projects (Conversations/ProjectsSection.tsx `embedded`, UnifiedSidebar/EfProjectsPanel.tsx, useUnifiedSidebarLinks):
  a panel of their own in place of the section above the history: «New project», the projects with their chats, and
  «All projects» (the upstream /projects page). The collapsed rail and the panel shortcuts include it. With a mouse, a
  project's name keeps the whole row until the row is hovered or focused (its actions show then).
- Admin-only display (useUnifiedSidebarLinks): employees do not see the agent builder or the parameters in the column,
  the rail or the shortcuts (owner decision while the owner learns them). Role permissions are unchanged.
- Composer hint (hooks/Input/useTextarea.ts): the empty box says «… or type / for a ready command» when the «/»
  command is on and the employee may use prompts.
- Chat titles (Conversations/ConvoLink.tsx): the overflow fade follows the title's own direction. postcss-preset-env
  rewrites `:dir(rtl)` as `[dir=rtl] &` (the page's direction), so an English title in the Arabic interface lost its
  first letters to the fade.
- Ready commands panel (Prompts/buttons/AutoSendPrompt.tsx): the «auto-send» button shows its state with a drawn box
  instead of a second (hidden) checkbox control nested in the button (axe nested-interactive); aria-pressed is unchanged.

